            <ArticleTitle>[The colistin MIC determination in Acinetobacter baumannii, Should it be reviewed?]</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-414</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0716-10182017000400413</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4067/s0716-10182017000400413</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Currently, there is a controversy in how to determine the minimal inhibitory concentration (MIC) of colistin against Acinetobacter baumannii. We compared three methods, concluding that the addition of Tween-80 (0.002%) to Müller-Hinton broth in the microdilution method could improve MIC determination and it could reduce false resistance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
